  "id": "visual-evoked-potential",
  "term": "visual evoked potential",
  "definition": "A visual evoked potential is the recorded time-based electrical response in the visual cortex after a visual stimulus. Its waveform features, such as the timing and size of peaks, can change with disease, and it may also contain more complex irregular patterns of uncertain significance.",
